  <h2>How to Season Jerky: Wet vs. Dry</h2>
  <p>Both wet marinades and dry rubs work — the choice comes down to flavor depth vs. surface texture. If you want the crusted, no-marinade style, start with the <a href="/beef-jerky-dry-rub/">best dry rub recipe for beef jerky</a>.</p>

