  <h2>Salt: The One Non-Negotiable Variable</h2>
  <p>Salt is the only ingredient in beef jerky seasoning that genuinely cannot be omitted or reduced significantly. It serves as a preservative (water activity reduction), a flavor amplifier, and a texture modifier. Too little salt produces jerky that spoils within days and tastes flat. Too much salt makes the finished jerky inedibly salty.</p>
  <p>The correct range is <strong>1 to 1.5 teaspoons of kosher salt per pound of raw beef</strong>. If you're using soy sauce as part of your marinade (3 tbsp soy = approximately 1.5 tsp salt equivalent), account for that sodium in your total.</p>

  <h2>Jerky Seasoning Recipe for Ground Meat</h2>
  <p>Ground meat jerky needs its seasoning mixed through the meat rather than soaked in — so the blend is drier and slightly stronger per pound. For 1 lb of 90/10 lean ground beef: 1 tsp garlic powder, 1 tsp onion powder, 1 tsp black pepper, 1 tsp smoked paprika, 1/2 tsp sea salt, 2 tbsp soy sauce, 1 tbsp Worcestershire, and 1/4 tsp Prague Powder No. 1.</p>
  <p>The curing salt is <strong>not optional for ground meat</strong> — grinding distributes surface bacteria through the entire mass, so ground jerky needs the nitrite protection that whole-muscle strips can skip. Mix thoroughly, rest 4–12 hours refrigerated, then pipe and dry. Full technique in the <a href="/ground-beef-jerky/">ground beef jerky guide</a>.</p>

  <h2>Best Store-Bought Jerky Seasoning Kits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Hi Mountain Jerky Seasonings</strong> — widest variety (15+ flavors), includes cure packet, designed for consistent home results. Best overall value.</li>
    <li><strong>LEM Products Backwoods</strong> — accurate pre-measured ratios, cure included, popular with hunters for wild game jerky.</li>
    <li><strong>Nesco Jerky Seasoning & Cure</strong> — designed to work with Nesco dehydrators, widely available at Walmart and hardware stores.</li>
    <li><strong>McCormick Bag 'N Season Beef Jerky</strong> — basic entry-level option, no cure packet, good for beginners who want simplicity.</li>
  </ul>

