  <h2>Curing Salt: Do You Need It?</h2>
  <p>Prague Powder #1 (sodium nitrite) prevents <em>Clostridium botulinum</em> (botulism) in low-oxygen environments — exactly what jerky becomes after vacuum sealing. Use it if you plan to store jerky longer than 2 weeks or vacuum-seal portions. The dose is exact: <strong>1/4 teaspoon per pound of raw meat</strong>. Do not increase this amount.</p>
  <p>For same-week consumption from a clean dehydrator at 160°F, curing salt is optional. For anything going in long-term storage or being gifted to others, include it.</p>
